\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, JULY 11, 2007\r\rMayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:31 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Coroalles, Lysik, Peirce, Permaul, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Dr. Don Zimring.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Assistant City Attorney Permaul announced that the City Council adjourned the June 20, 2007 City Council meeting into closed session and the City Council authorized the City Attorney to defend the City in an action entitled Keeler v. the City of Calabasas.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor Bozajian announced that Dr. Don Zimring has recently taken the position of Superintendent for the Las Virgenes Unified School District. Mayor Bozajian introduced Jennifer Bercy and Sharon Boucher, 2007 Calabasas Relay for Life Event Co-Chairs, and presented them with proclamations in recognition of their service. Mayor Bozajian presented a proclamation to Marlee Elizabeth Pelta in recognition of her perfect attendance in high school. Councilmember Groveman congratulated organizers and staff on the successful Relay for Life Event. Councilmember Wolfson congratulated Dr. Zimring on his new role as Superintendent of Las Virgenes Unified School District and congratulated staff for the successful 4th of July events. Mayor pro Tem Maurer also congratulated Dr. Zimring on his recent appointment and introduced the new Principal of Calabasas High School, Vince Jantz. Mayor pro Tem Maurer spoke regarding upcoming events taking place at the King Gillette Ranch property. Councilmember Washburn also congratulated Dr. Zimring and announced that the new Chamber of Commerce Business and Community Directory is being distributed throughout the City. Mayor Bozajian announced several upcoming events: Las Virgenes Creek Restoration Ribbon Cutting Ceremony on July 18 and several Movie events in the park.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Evan Kroll, Sam Platter and Kane Rhee, Calabasas, spoke regarding introducing a skate park in the City of Calabasas. Lynda Caiati, Calabasas, spoke regarding the Calabasas High School track. Hal Helsley, Calabasas, spoke regarding watering at A.C. Stelle Middle School and the recent roadway improvements to Mulholland Highway.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r \r Approval of the minutes for the June 13, 2007 and June 20, 2007 City Council meetings and June 16, 2007 Budget Workshop.\r\r Approval of a contract with Olivas Valdez, Inc. in the amount of $1,126,200 for the construction of Las Virgenes Creek Restoration Project and a professional services agreement with Questa Engineering Corporation in the amount not to exceed $40,000 for overseeing and inspecting the same project.\r\r Approval of a professional service agreement between the City of Calabasas and the Las Virgenes Municipal Water District to prepare the final report for the Malibu Creek Watershed Monitoring Program.\r\r Budget adjustment for All-America City Award presentation and participation expenses for fiscal year 2006-2007.\r\r Approval of contract with Camarillo Engineering, Inc. for repair of City-owned storm drains prior to transfer to Los Angeles County.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1096, \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015approving a salary schedule for hourly employees.\r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2007-236 for video service providers operating with a state franchise.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to approve Consent Item #1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Recommendation to award a construction contract to TDS Engineering in the amount of $161,288 for a new traffic signal installation at Old Topanga Canyon Road and Mulholland Highway (Project Specification No. 06-07-15); and to authorize expenditures for the traffic signal installation. \r\rRobert Yalda, Public Works Director/City Engineer and Marc Seferian, Senior Civil Engineer, presented the staff report.\r\rAssistant City Attorney Permaul spoke regarding the proceedings for the discussion in regards to pending litigation on the traffic signal installation.\r\rKaren Sobel, Calabasas, Gary Klein, Calabasas, representing the Calabasas Hills Homeowners Association, Dr. Donald Zimring, Superintendent, Las Virgenes Unified School District, Paul Rosenbaum, Executive Director, Viewpoint School, Debra Gibson, Calabasas, Robert Pope, representing the Calabasas Park Homeowners Association, John Eisz, Calabasas Highlands, Ron Tinero, Oak Creek Estates, Michelle and Norman Dornfest, Calabasas Highlands, Chris Godfrey, Calabasas, Michael Newfield, Traffic & Transportation Commission, Sergeant Brooks, Los Angeles County Sheriff�s Department, Lost Hills Sheriff�s Station, spoke in support of the award of the contract for the proposed traffic signal installation. Nancy Rothenberg, Calabasas Highlands, Hal Helsley, Calabasas, Elizabeth, Robert and Brittany Stephens, Calabasas Highlands, Bob Benson, Calabasas Highlands, Bruce Benson, Calabasas Highlands, Toby Keeler, Topanga, Cynthia Maxwell, Calabasas, Shelly Palmer, Calabasas, Leon Koziewicz, Mary Hubbard, representing Las Virgenes Homeowners Federation, spoke in opposition to the award of the contract for the proposed traffic signal installation. Gary Walch, representing Oak Creek Estates Homeowners Association, spoke in support of the traffic signal installation as long as the installation does not cause additional congestion with the traffic signals at Bluebird Drive and Park Ora. Ted DePass, Calabasas, expressed concern that the funds are being spent from the General Fund. \r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to award the construction contract to TDS Engineering. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r The City Council recessed at 9:47 p.m. and reconvened at 10:02 p.m.\r\r Discussion regarding the Draft Regional Housing Needs Assessment Allocation 2006-2014.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\r\r\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r \r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1098, approving the Operating and Capital Improvement Budget for July 1, 2007 through June 30, 2009, providing for the appropriations and expenditures for all sums set forth in said budget; and adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1099, establishing the appropriations limit for fiscal year 2007-2008.\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rDr. Gary J. Lysik, Chief Financial Officer, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1098, approving the Operating and Capital Improvement Budget for FY 2007-08 and 2008-09. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1100, finding the City of Calabasas to be in conformance with the congestion management program, and adopting the local development report, in accordance with California Government Code Section 65089.\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1100, finding the City in conformance with the congestion management program and adopting the local development report. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of June 14, 2007 to June 21, 2007.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Maurer spoke regarding a recent Santa Monica Mountains Conservancy meeting.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Maurer requested information on permitting of illegal dumpsters and an item for the Education Fund. \r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 10:45 p.m.\r \r\r\r______________________________\rRobin Parker, City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 3 -\u0015\r07/11/07\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0001\b\u0000\u0000\u0015\b\u0000\u0000\u0016\b\u0000\u0000q\b\u0000\u0000r\b\u0000\u0000}\b\u0000\u0000\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000\u001a \u0000\u0000# \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000���ǹ������y�m^m^K^m^m^m\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%\u0015hiy\f\u0000\u0016h�\n�\u00005\b�>*\u0001OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000\\\b�^J\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u001c\u0015hiy\f\u0000\u0016h�\n�\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000^J\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u0000\u0016\u0016h�\n�\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000^J\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u0000\u001b\u0015h�z�\u0000\u0016h�.3\u00005\b�OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u001b\u0015h�z�\u0000\u0016h^TV\u00005\b�OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u0015\u0016h\ff\u0000\u00005\b�OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u00